window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Nothing about her world is as she believed it to be . . .</b></p> <p>When Woodside fell, Remy Angellette and her friends barely escaped with their lives and were left scrambling to find a new place to call home. But Brandt Evans is missing, taken by the very people he called for help. Remy is determined to find him, but she doesn't know where to start looking. And to make matters worse, she's dealing with strange side effects from the cure to the Michaluk Virus that could endanger them all.</p> <p>As Remy and her friends set out on a mission to find Brandt, she resolves to do everything in her power to locate him—or die trying. The search takes her back into the heart of Atlanta, into the very city where her life changed. And what she finds there are seeds of a betrayal she didn't expect and a world wholly different than what she and her friends believed it to be after the Michaluk Virus struck.</p> <p>With her world turned on its head and her infection symptoms getting worse, Remy finds herself dealing with the biggest challenge of her life . . . and she has no idea if she's going to survive it.</p> <p>Contains mature themes.</p>"; 
